Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:14:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 108/162] hjviewer: one dialog frame, one button and the core's
 toasts (UX-S2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U51: hjvButton (dialog.dart) over hjv_style.dart's pure hjvButtonFor and
hjvButtonLook, with the tones primary, quiet, alt and danger and the sizes
normal, screen (40) and form (44). dialogButton, hjvDangerButton and the
_button copies of the access, account and update screens call it, their
signatures kept. The desktop theme's Elevated, Outlined and Text buttons are
at least 36 high, 16 at the sides, at the standard density
(kHjvDesktopButton); the settings' two local 36 px styles point at it.
HjvCallout's actions keep the theme's density, so the notices keep their
heights.

U10: on a phone, another way (alt) is a text button in the accent's colour
at 600: A1's and A0's [로그인] with the field open, the login notice's
[이 PC 빼기]. [취소] stays grey, [연결] bold.

U50: the two frames (alert, form) are written down in dialog.dart.
HjvDialogWidth sm 360 / md 440 / lg 560 goes to contentBoxConstraints: md
for A1, A2, A0, LK1, the PC home's close question, the PC password dialog,
the session's message boxes, the account's dialogs; lg for the update
screen and the login notice; sm for delete and rename. msgboxContent puts
a 22 px icon on the title's line and the text below it at the full width
in 14/1.5. The update dialog is an alert: the texts at the left, [닫기]
then the other buttons and the main one last at the right.

U45 (the rest): the core's text toasts (FfiModel.handleToast) go through
showToast; an error gets an error icon in the inverse theme's danger text
colour (HjvToast's danger).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
